w2c2/PATCHES.md-6-   `f32_reinterpret_i32(0x..)` / `f64_reinterpret_i64(0x..)`. Upstream printed
w2c2/PATCHES.md-7-   finite non-negative-zero values with `%.9g` / `%.17g`, which (a) needs a
w2c2/PATCHES.md-8-   correct decimal float printer in the guest libc and (b) is a platform
w2c2/PATCHES.md-9-   nondeterminism source. Hex is exact and identical everywhere.
w2c2/PATCHES.md-10-2. `stringbuilder.c/.h`: removed `stringBuilderAppendF32/F64` (only users of float printf).
w2c2/PATCHES.md-11-3. `main.c`: the "%.2f%%" statistic on stderr in the reference-module path is now an integer message.
w2c2/PATCHES.md-12-4. `main.c` `wasmFunctionIDsCompareHashes`: tie-break on function index. Functions
w2c2/PATCHES.md-13-   are emitted in hash order; identical bodies hash equal, so the emitted order of
w2c2/PATCHES.md:14:   duplicates depended on the platform qsort's stability (glibc mergesort: stable;
w2c2/PATCHES.md-15-   musl smoothsort: not). Now a total order.
w2c2/PATCHES.md-16-5. `main.c` `cleanImplementationFiles`: without glob/Win32 the function is a no-op
w2c2/PATCHES.md-17-   instead of `#error` (the wasm guest has no directory listing).
